From: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-arduino-monza: enable the USB link to the MCU

The STM32 MCU is connected to usb_2 (the Bridge to Linux and gs_usb CAN),
but the host never sees it: PMIC GPIO 7 (usb2-en) stays low. Arduino's
Ubuntu image drives it high from usb_2's default pin state. Do the same.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Stefano Viola <stefano.viola@toradex.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
@@ -450,6 +450,16 @@
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 23 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 };
 
+&pmm8650au_1_gpios {
+	/* Enables the USB link to the MCU, as on Arduino's images */
+	usb2_en: usb2-en-state {
+		pins = "gpio7";
+		function = "normal";
+		output-high;
+		power-source = <0>;
+	};
+};
+
 &thermal_zones {
 	cpuss-0-0-thermal {
 		polling-delay = <2000>;
@@ -606,6 +616,9 @@
 
 /* Internally connected to the MCU (e.g. for DFU). */
 &usb_2 {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&usb2_en>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+
 	dr_mode = "host";
 
 	status = "okay";
